 tags on `mimo` models and the fact that `openai-codex` still appears despite being removed from `models.json` indicates the gateway hasn't reloaded the updated configuration yet. Restarting the gateway would likely refresh what the CLI is reading. The issue is that `doubao` models aren't showing up in the CLI output even though they're defined in the config files. Looking at the provider structure, I notice the `doubao` models use `input: [\"text\", \"image\"]` format while `bujing` models use `input: [\"text\"]` - this difference in how the input field is structured might be causing the CLI to filter them out or not recognize them properly.\n\nSince the gateway appears to be using cached config, I should restart it first to ensure it's reading the current state, then investigate why the `doubao` models specifically aren't displaying in the list.","thinkingSignature":"fa126aa6472ace6faceec94377a76fb2e7f41b157fc77e3402c466abd49e2074"},{"type":"text","text":"1. ✅ mimo 已删除\n2. 发现了配置不一致的问题：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_nv2tazoy0tr7_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"echo \"=== CLI still showing removed stuff - checking if gateway needs restart ===\"\necho \"\"\necho \"models.json still has openai-codex:\"\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nd = json.load(open('/root/.openclaw/agents/main/agent/models.json'))\nprint('  providers:', list(d['providers'].keys()))\n\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"openclaw.json has:\"\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nd = json.load(open('/root/.openclaw/openclaw.json'))\nprint('  providers:', list(d['models']['providers'].keys()))\nprint('  defaults.models:', list(d['agents']['defaults']['models'].keys()))\n\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== doubao provider details ===\"\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nd = json.load(open('/root/.openclaw/agents/main/agent/models.json'))\nprint(json.dumps(d['providers'].get('doubao', 'NOT FOUND'), indent=2))\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":97568,"output":1