{"type":"message","id":"e8bad34e","parentId":"68a0b2b5","timestamp":"2026-03-26T14:35:49.766Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The CLI is still showing the old cached data - `mimo` is still there and `openai-codex` is still there even though I removed them from the files. This is because the gateway is still running with the old config in memory.\n\nThe issue is that `openclaw gateway restart` keeps getting killed before it completes. This is because the current session (the CLI I'm running in) is connected through the gateway, so when the gateway restarts, the process gets a SIGTERM.\n\nThis is a common issue with gateway restarts while connected through it. The restart works, but the current exec session gets terminated.\n\nThe models list shows the cached state from before the changes. \n\nI can verify that the config files are correct though - the provider removals are actually persisted in both openclaw.json and models.json, but the gateway needs to restart to load the new configuration and reflect those changes in the CLI output.","thinkingSignature":"4748487a28cc31db20e3fb349c99967aa11cf1c3f84cdd57a0196a60de73cf52"},{"type":"text","text":"Gateway 重启时会把当前连接打断，所以命令一直被 SIGTERM。\n\n**已确认的状态：**\n\n**✅ 配置文件已更新：**\n- mimo: 已从 `openclaw.json` 和 `models.json` 删除\n- openai-codex: 已从 `models.json` 删除\n- doubao、arkcode、minimax、bujing 全部正常\n\n**❌ CLI 显示的是 Gateway 内存里的旧缓存**，重启后才能刷新。\n\n你需要手动在另一个终端执行：\n```bash\nopenclaw gateway restart\n```\n重启后 CLI 列表就会显示干净的配置：doubao、arkcode、minimax、bujing 四个 provider。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":98936,"output":325,"cacheRead":22134,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":121395,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774535740171}}
